Which overload is called by each line?
```cpp
void f(const Cloud&) { std::cout << "L"; }
void f(Cloud&&)      { std::cout << "R"; }

Cloud c(10);
f(c);
f(Cloud(5));
f(std::move(c));
```

What prints?
```cpp
void g(const Cloud&) { std::cout << "L"; }
void g(Cloud&&)      { std::cout << "R"; }
void h(Cloud&& c)     { g(c); }

h(Cloud(3));
```

Which call fails to compile?
```cpp
void scale(Cloud& c, double s);
Cloud load();

Cloud a = load();
scale(a, 2.0);          // (A)
scale(load(), 2.0);     // (B)
const Cloud& r = load();// (C)
scale(a, 2);            // (D)
```

How many times is `Cloud`'s copy constructor called? (C++17, with optimisations off)
```cpp
